	  <tr bgcolor="#CCFF99">
	    <td align="center" bgcolor="#CCFFFF"><div align="left">Weekly Challenge #4a</div></td>
	    <td bgcolor="#CCFFFF">Terminal Value</td>
	    <td bgcolor="#CCFFFF"><a href="wkch/wkch4a.htm">Weekly challenge</a><br>
	      <a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pc/wkch/wkch4asol.xls">Solution</a></td>
      </tr>
	  <tr bgcolor="#CCFF99">
	    <td align="left" bgcolor="#CCFFFF"><a href="https://youtu.be/An2SduBDYQE?si=lI-5O4vnjEBd9t26">Valuation Tools Webcast #8<br>
Estimating accounting returns (ROE, ROIC)</a><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/podcasts/Webcasts/ROIC.mp4"></a></td>
	    <td bgcolor="#CCFFFF">In assessing whether a company's existing investments are good or not, we draw on accounting return measures: return on invested capital and return on equity. However, navigating what should be in invested capital and what should not, and how to adjust for accounting inconsistencies is tricky. </td>
	    <td bgcolor="#CCFFFF"><ol>
	      <li><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/cfovhds/webcasts/ROIC/walmart10K.pdf">Walmart 10K (2013)</a></li>
	      <li><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/cfovhds/webcasts/ROIC/walmart10Klastyear.pdf">Walmart 10K (2012)</a></li>
	      <li><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/cfovhds/webcasts/ROIC/walmartreturncalculator.xls">Spreadsheet</a></li>
	      </ol></td>
      </tr>
	  <tr bgcolor="#FFFFCC">
	    <td align="center" bgcolor="#CCFFFF"><div align="left"><a href="https://youtu.be/JW-S4BVSZV0?si=-SiktApRHyrrc1Dq">Valuation Tools Webcast #9 (Checking Terminal Value)</a><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/podcasts/Webcasts/terminalvalue.mp4"></a></div></td>
	    <td bgcolor="#CCFFFF">The terminal value is a &quot;big&quot; number in DCF valuation, but it is subject to misuse and manipuluation. In this session, I take a look at how you can detect problems with a terminal value computation (in both your own DCFs and in other people's DCFs)</td>
	    <td bgcolor="#CCFFFF"><a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/eqnotes/webcasts/TermValueCheck/termvalueDCF.xls">Sample DCF valuation</a><br>
	      <a href="https://www.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/eqnotes/webcasts/TermValueCheck/termvaluecheck.xls">Terminal value analyzer</a></td>
      </tr>
